      "seconds_since_start": 9.315,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.096
    },
    "text": "This is exactly the kind of Lake Formation authorization-chain diagnosis I can run \u2014 tracing LF grants, resource links, IAM, S3 bucket policy, and KMS to find the exact layer blocking the EMR job, read-only start to finish.\n\nTo run the diagnosis I need a few specifics I can't guess:\n\n1. **EMR execution role ARN** (or the EMR cluster ID \u2014 I can look up the role from that)\n2. **Target table**: catalog database/table name (and the account/region it lives in)\n3. **Account/region** of the EMR job itself, if different (cross-account access)\n4. Optionally, the exact error message or CloudTrail request ID from the failed Spark job, if you have it handy\n\nIf it's easier, just give me the cluster ID and the database.table name and I'll pull the rest."
  },
